Ten seconds into a pause (or a stop) the outputs are stopped: TEARDOWN
to every AirPlay device, the event channel closed. A HomePod whose
sender has gone treats its next tap as "play something" and starts the
household's own library, and the sender's resume then finds the speaker
busy. Kept, the session stays the HomePod's current one, a tap comes
back over the event channel as a play command, and resume is a restart
of the stream, not a fresh connect.

So the sessions are kept until something real ends them: the user
switching the speaker off, or another sender taking it, which the app
already handles by rejoining once it is free. A year stands in for
never; the timer wants a number.

--- a/src/outputs.c
+++ b/src/outputs.c
@@ -86,7 +86,7 @@
 // actually just restarting. This timeout determines how long we wait before
 // full stop.
 // (value is in seconds)
-#define OUTPUTS_STOP_TIMEOUT 10
+#define OUTPUTS_STOP_TIMEOUT (365 * 24 * 3600)
 
 #define OUTPUTS_MAX_CALLBACKS 64
 
